{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"The exact two-pass version is numerically excellent (over 99.9% matched even under deliberately harsh unscaled random weights), but recomputing QK and `tanh` makes long contexts slower. I’m keeping its exact normalization while caching only the final BF16 logits inside the same kernel; that trades cheap HBM traffic for removing the entire second QK/softcap pass."}}
